<title>ESTONIA: BALTIC 30 INDEX DOWN 1.39 PCT TO 108.7.</title>
<headline>BALTIC 30 INDEX DOWN 1.39 PCT TO 108.7.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic 30 index, the only pan-Baltic index, which is compiled by the three leading business newspapers, fell by 1.39 percent to 108.70 on Friday, Estonia's Aripaev said.</p>
<p>The Baltic 30 index covers the 10 leading stocks from the three Baltic stock markets and is compiled by Aripaev, Lithuania's Verslo Zinios and Latvia's Dienas Bizness.</p>
<p>The index started from 100 on May 19.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom, +372 620 9202/1, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
